{"id":"word:hebrew:H2534","type":"word","title":"חֵמָה","subtitle":"H2534 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"heat ; figuratively, anger , poison (from its fever)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to חֵמָה (H2534) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-f.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 124 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"חֵמָה (chêmâh) means heat ; figuratively, anger , poison (from its fever) First listed occurrence: 2Chr 12 7."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"חֵמָה","transliteration":"chêmâh","pronunciation":"khay-maw'","strong":"H2534","lemmaId":"hebrew:H2534","partOfSpeech":"n-f","forms":["חֲמַת","חֲמָתִ/י֙","חֲמַ֣ת","חֲמָתִ֖/י","חֵ֭מָה"],"morphs":[["HNcfsc/Sp1cs",26],["HNcfsa",21],["HNcfsc",19],["HR/Ncfsa",8],["HC/R/Ncfsa",6],["HNcfsc/Sp2ms",6],["HNcfsc/Sp3ms",6],["HC/R/Ncfsc/Sp1cs",5],["HR/Ncfsc",4],["HR/Ncfsc/Sp1cs",3]]},"definitions":{"short":"heat ; figuratively, anger , poison (from its fever)","usage":"anger, bottles, hot displeasure, furious(-ly, -ry), heat, indignation, poison, rage, wrath(-ful). See 2529 .","full":"H2534. chemah חֵמָא see חֵמָה below יחם . חֵמָה wrath , see below יחם ; חֵמָה Job 29:6 , see חֶמְאָה ; חַמַּת חַמּוֺן, חַמָּן, חַמָּה, see below חמם . below חֵמָה (once חֵמָא ):121 noun feminine heat, rage (for ֗֗֗ יְחֵמָה ; Late Hebrew id. ; Aramaic יַחְמָא poison , heat, wrath, poison , Brock Lex. 116 , also Nö § 103 ; Arabic poison , Lane 651 ; Assyrian imtu, spittle, breath , poison , Dl HWB 78 Muss-Arn CD 62 ) — absolute חֵמָה Nahum 1:2 39t.; חֵמָא Dan 11:44 ; construct חֲמַת Gen 27:44 25 t.; suffix חֲמָתִי Jer 4:4 36t.; חֲמָֽתְךָ 10:25 8 t.; חֲמָתֶ֑ךָ Psa 88:8 ; 89:47 ; חֲמָתוֺ Isa 51:17 8 t.; חֲמָתָם Job 6:4 ; plural חֵמוֺת Prov 22:24 , חֵמֹת Psa 76:11 ; &#8212; 1 heat: a. fever , מִיַּיִן חֲמַת Hosea 7:5 fever from wine, wine-fever (on stative construct see Ges § 130 , 1). b. venom, poison (figurative): עָפָר זֹחֲלֵי חֲמַת Deut 32:24 ; ׳ח תַּנִּינִים 32:33 ; ׳ח נָחָשׁ Psa 58:5 compare 58:5 ; ׳ח עַכְשׁוּב 140:4 ; poison of arrows (of ׳י ) Job 6:4 . 2 burning anger, rage: a. of man: Gen 27:44 (J), 2Sam 11:20 ; 2Kin 5:12 ; Est 1:12 ; 2:1 ; 3:5 ; 5:9 (against, עַל ), 7:7 , 10 ; Psa 37:8 (|| אַף ), 76:11 (yet on text see Che), Prov 6:34 ; 15:1 , 18 ( חֵמָה אִישׁ man of rage = raging or wrathful man), 16:4 ; 19:19 ( ׳גְּדָלאח Qr = one great in rage , see De Now), 27:4 (|| אַף ), Isa 51:13 (twice in verse); Ezek 23:25 ; חֵמוֺת אִישׁ Prov 22:24 (|| אָ֑ף בַּעַל ); חֵמָה בַּעַל 29:22 (|| אַף אִישׁ ); עַזָּה חֵמָה strong rage 21:14 (|| אַף ); רוּחִי חֲמַת Ezek 3:14 the rage of my spirit. b. of the he-goat in Daniel's vision , כֹחוֺ בַּחֲמַת Dan 8:6 in the fury of his power. c. of God ( ׳י ), often Jeremiah, Isa 2 , Ezekiel, Psalms: Jer 4:4 16 t. Jeremiah; 2Kin 22:13 , 17 ; Isa 27:4 (Hi Ew Di Du; on other interpretations, and on text see Di), 63:5 ; Lam 2:4 ; Ezek 5:13 29t. Ezekiel; Num 25:11 (P), 2Chr 12:7 ; 34:21 , 25 ; 36:16 ; Psa 59:14 ; 79:6 ; 88:8 ; 89:47 ; 106:23 ; Job 21:20 ; apparently also 19:29 ; 36:18 see Di; often || אַף Micah 5:14 ; Deut 9:19 ; 29:22 ; Isa 42:25 ( אַמּוֺ as appositive, + מִלְחָמָה עֱזוּז ), 63:3 , 6 ; Dan 9:16 ; Psa 6:2 ; 78:38 ; 90:7 ; אַמּוֺ בְּחֵמָה לְהָשִׁיב 66:15 (|| בְּלַהֲבֵיאֵֿשׁ וְגַעֲרַתוֺ ), + Jer 23:19 ; 30:23 of the whirlwind of ׳י ; || אַף + גָּדוֺל קֶצֶף Deut 29:27 ; Jer 21:5 ; 32:37 ; || אַף + חֵמָה תֹּכְחוֺת Ezek 5:15 , compare חֵמָה תּוֺכְחוֺת alone 25:17 ; || אַמּוֺ חֲרוֺן Nahum 1:6 ; Lam 4:11 ; || קֶצֶף Isa 34:2 (of fury against, על ), Psa 38:2 ; || גְּעָרָה Isa 51:20 ; || גְּמוּל 59:18 ; || קִנְאָה Ezek 36:6 , compare קִנֵּאתִי גְדוֺלָה חֵמָה Zech 8:2 (|| גדולה קִנְאָה ); וְקִנְאָה חֵמָה דַּם Ezek 16:38 (on text see Co); קֶ֑רִי חֲמַת Lev 26:28 rage of meeting , i.e. encountering them in rage ; חֲמָתוֺ(ת־ִיׅ כּוֺס Isa 51:17 , 22 the cup of his (my) fury ; הַזּאֹת הַחֵמָה הַיַּיִן כּוֺס Jer 25:15 ; חֵמָה בַּעַל a possessor of fury = furious Nahum 1:2 (|| קִנּוֺא אֵל נֹקֵם, ). [ עַל חֵמָה = rage against one: Isa 34:2 ; 2Chr 28:9 . — Vbs. used with חֵמָה are: 2. a.: שׁוּב Gen 27:44 , הֵשִׁיב Prov 15:1 , עָלָה 2Sam 11:20 , בָּעַר Est 1:12 , שָׁכַךְ 2:1 ; 7:10 ; 2. c.: הֵשִׁיב turn away wrath of ׳י Num 25:11 ; Psa 106:23 ; Jer 18:20 (but אַמּוֺ בְּחֵמָה הָשִׁיכ Isa 66:15 to recompense his anger in fury , give it as requital); ׳ח ׳י is kindled against one ב יצת Niph`al 2Kin 22:13 , 17 ; it burns בָּֽעֲרָה Jer 4:4 ; 21:12 ; 44:6 ; Psa 89:47 ; arises עלה 2Chr 36:16 , compare as object of עלה Hiph`il Ezek 24:8 ; is poured out בְ נִתְּכָה 2Chr 12:7 ; 34:21 , 25 ; Jer 7:20 ; עַל נִתְּכָה 42:18 (twice in verse); 44:6 ; כָאֵשׁ נִתְּכָה Nahum 1:6 ; ׳י pours it out אֶל שָׁפַךְ Psa 79:6 ; עַל שָׁפַךְ Isa 42:25 ; Jer 10:25 ; Ezek 7:8 ; 9:8 ; 14:19 ; 16:38 (according to Co's conjecture), 20:8 , 13 , 21 ; 22:22 ; 30:15 ; 36:18 ; כָּאֵשׁ שָׁפַךְ Lam 2:4 ; שְׁפוּכָה חֵמָה Ezek 20:33-34 , ח ׳הֵנִיחַ בְ bring to rest (i.e. satisfy) one's fury upon 5:13 ; 16:42 ; 24:13 ; ח ׳כִּלָּה Lam 4:11 ; + בְּ Ezek 5:13 I have accomplished my fury upon them (in their case), 6:12 ; 13:15 .] יַחְמוּר see below IV. חמר יַחְמַי see below חמה יחף (√ of following; original meaning unknown; Late Hebrew Aramaic יָחֵף adjective as Hebrew; Syriac Aph`el discalceatus fuit ; compare perhaps Arabic (transposed) walk barefoot , also become chafed , of foot or hoof). יחם (√ of following; see Biblical Hebrew יָחַם , whence חֵמָה ).","rootNote":"or (Daniel 11:44) חֵמָא ; from 3179 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"2Chr 12 7","keyReferences":["2Chr 12 7","2Chr 28 9","2Chr 34 21","2Chr 34 25","2Chr 36 16","2Kgs 5 12","2Kgs 22 13","2Kgs 22 17"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":124,"occurrences":[{"reference":"2Chr 12 7","book":"2Chr","chapter":12,"verse":7,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"חֲמָתִ֛/י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcfsc/Sp1cs"},{"reference":"2C